1
00:00:00,255 --> 00:00:04,055
(Sheldon:)In the pre-Christian era, as the winter
solstice approached and the plants died...

2
00:00:04,217 --> 00:00:08,097
...pagans brought evergreen boughs in their
homes as an act of sympathetic magic...

3
00:00:08,263 --> 00:00:11,473
(Sheldon:)...intended to guard the life essences
of the plants until spring.

4
00:00:11,641 --> 00:00:14,101
This custom was appropriated
by northern Europeans...

5
00:00:14,269 --> 00:00:17,269
(Sheldon:)...and, eventually, it becomes
the so-called Christmas tree.

6
00:00:18,982 --> 00:00:22,982
(Howard:)And that, Charlie Brown,
is what boredom is all about.

7
00:00:24,863 --> 00:00:28,493
(Penny:)Okay, well, thank you for that.
I got you and Leonard silly neighbor gifts...

8
00:00:28,658 --> 00:00:31,498
(Penny:)- ...so I'll just put them under my tree.
- Wait.

9
00:00:31,661 --> 00:00:33,831
(Sheldon:)- You bought me a present?
- Uh-huh.

10
00:00:33,997 --> 00:00:35,957
(Sheldon:)Why would you do such a thing?

11
00:00:36,917 --> 00:00:39,457
- I don't know. Because it's Christmas?
- Oh, Penny.

12
00:00:39,628 --> 00:00:41,208
(Sheldon:)I know you think you're being generous...

13
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:43,960
(Sheldon:)...but the foundation of gift-giving
is reciprocity.

14
00:00:44,132 --> 00:00:48,182
(Sheldon:)You haven't given me a gift,
you've given me an obligation.

15
00:00:49,554 --> 00:00:52,304
(Howard:)Don't feel bad, Penny.
It's a classic rookie mistake.

16
00:00:52,474 --> 00:00:55,644
(Howard:)My first Hanukkah with Sheldon,
he yelled at me for eight nights.

17
00:00:58,063 --> 00:01:00,143
(Penny:)It's okay.
You don't have to get me anything.

